WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.105
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit 9:
Thinking, Feelings, and Imagination.

2
00:00:05.185 --> 00:00:11.875
This last unit of Year 3 explores the world
inside your head: thinking, feeling and imagining.

3
00:00:11.955 --> 00:00:19.581
You will learn sixteen words for ideas and emotions,
including idea, sense, reason, sadness and experience.

4
00:00:19.661 --> 00:00:27.864
You will practise imagining, making a choice, giving a
reason with because, and suggesting ideas kindly in a group.

5
00:00:27.944 --> 00:00:35.786
In the story The Box of Ideas, children at a school by
the sea fill a special box with their dreams and hopes.

6
00:00:35.866 --> 00:00:41.835
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:41.915 --> 00:00:49.306
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
use abstract nouns like idea, reason, experience,

8
00:00:49.386 --> 00:00:53.120
and sadness to talk about thoughts and feelings.

9
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:59.001
You will also say what you imagine
and describe the pictures in your mind.

10
00:00:59.081 --> 00:01:03.451
You will also give a reason for something using because.

11
00:01:03.531 --> 00:01:06.392
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:01:06.472 --> 00:01:12.499
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
idea, imagine, reason, purpose, choice, sense.

13
00:01:12.579 --> 00:01:17.875
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

14
00:01:17.955 --> 00:01:22.057
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

15
00:01:22.137 --> 00:01:28.141
The reading sequence includes The Box of Ideas
at School and Feelings Are Not Bad or Good.

16
00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.087
Read actively.

17
00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:33.752
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

18
00:01:33.832 --> 00:01:38.146
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

19
00:01:38.226 --> 00:01:41.195
The first language focus is Abstract Nouns.

20
00:01:41.275 --> 00:01:48.713
An abstract noun names something you cannot see, touch,
or hold, such as a feeling, a quality, or an idea.

21
00:01:48.793 --> 00:01:53.889
Words like idea, experience, sadness
and kindness are all abstract nouns.

22
00:01:53.969 --> 00:01:58.783
They let you talk about what is
happening inside your mind and heart.

23
00:01:58.863 --> 00:02:06.513
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:10.588
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Share an Idea.

25
00:02:10.668 --> 00:02:15.295
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:15.375 --> 00:02:18.878
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:18.958 --> 00:02:22.601
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:22.681 --> 00:02:24.265
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:24.345 --> 00:02:31.425
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:31.505 --> 00:02:34.896
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:34.976 --> 00:02:42.924
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
